l steps to ensure a smooth transition\nto get started at USF. We offer these resources to provide guidance that can direct\nyou to the offices to best assist you. This journey involves immigration processes,\nvisa regulations, and student health insurance among other important considerations.\nWe hope these can expedite your learning curve.\nBefore You Arrive\nOffice of International Services\nAdmission Requirements\nHealth Insurance\nEnhance Your Experience\nOnce you are on campus, it is time to begin your academic exploration. Attend ITA\nSupport Workshops to enhance experience in your role. ITA Handbook outlines eligibility\nrequirements and language proficiency goals for international teaching assistants.\nITA Support\nITA Handbook\nUniversity of South Florida\nLocated in Tampa and St. Petersburg.\n4202 E. Fowler Avenue, ALN 226,\nTampa, FL 33620, USA\n813-974-2846\nConnect with us:\nFacebook\nX\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nAbout USF\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nLocations\nCampus Life\nResearch\nAdministrative Units\nRegulations & Policies\nHuman Resources\nWork at USF\nEmergency & Safety\nTitle IX\nGraduate Programs\nGraduate Certificates\nGraduate Catalog\nETD Resource Center\nOffice of Postdoctoral Affairs\nPostdoc Opportunities\nCopyright \u00a9 2026, University of South Florida. All rights reserved.\nThis website is maintained by Office of Graduate Studies.\nPrivacy\nContact USF\nVisit USF\nAccessibility", "links": [["Skip to Main Content", "https://www.usf.edu/graduate-studies/student-academics/international-resources/index.aspx#content"], ["University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956", "https://www.usf.edu"], ["University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956", "https://www.usf.edu"], ["Search", "https://cloud.usf.edu/search/"], ["Office of Graduate Studies", "https://www.usf.edu/graduate-studies/index.aspx"], ["Student Academics", "https://www.usf.edu/graduate-studies/student-academics/index.aspx"], ["Graduate School at USF", "https://www.usf.edu/graduate-studies/student-a